The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/der-catalog/dercat-10-pv-lut-sam-interpolation.md`.

**Summary**: 7 findings (0 critical, 2 high, 3 medium, 2 low):

| # | Severity | Issue |
|---|----------|-------|
| 1 | High | LUT indexed on month/hour instead of solar-position-aware dimensions — weather-file-specific, biased if reused across locations |
| 2 | High | Inverter efficiency double-counting and system losses silently ignored in LUT path (4-18% systematic over-estimate) |
| 3 | Medium | DEFAULT_NOCT=47°C doesn't match SAM's 45°C (open-rack) or 49°C (roof-mounted) |
| 4 | Medium | Multi-linear interpolation frequently falls through to nearest-neighbor due to sparse grid from weather-file-only points |
| 5 | Medium | Albedo not configurable; snow albedo adjustment missing |
| 6 | Low | No interpolation error documented or validated against direct SAM runs |
| 7 | Low | LUT generator uses `hour//730` month binning; consumer uses calendar months — mismatch at boundaries |
